            {
                "entry_id": "a32b223f-83a8-34d9-a26b-f8d2d44772c7",
                "word": "untime",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4d5e6d4c-d1cf-4503-8c5e-9c2b55c38574",
                        "entry_id": "a32b223f-83a8-34d9-a26b-f8d2d44772c7",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "untimes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9606747f-dc02-349c-8493-934c8cd74f51",
                        "entry_id": "a32b223f-83a8-34d9-a26b-f8d2d44772c7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The absence of time; timelessness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae11973a-67bf-4fc4-94de-653f15d2011c",
                                "sense_id": "9606747f-dc02-349c-8493-934c8cd74f51",
                                "text": "Actually, his apocalypse is a reverse cosmogony: he features himself as a monstrous Leviathan swallowing all the faithful, and the Untime celebrated by \"unceasing\" clock-chiming seals the reign of death and the return to pre-cosmogonic chaos. Death, not life, is what the imam has to offer to the faithful of Desh."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d21ea475-96d3-410a-a5b6-a165b95e712f",
                                "sense_id": "9606747f-dc02-349c-8493-934c8cd74f51",
                                "text": "The body of Al-Lat has shrivelled on the grass, leaving behind only a dark stain; and now every clock in the capital city of Desh begins to chime, and goes on unceasingly, beyond twelve, beyond twenty-four, beyond one thousand and one, announcing the end of Time, the hour that is beyond measuring, the hour of the exile's return, of the victory of water over wine, of the commencement of the Untime of the Imam."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "358392b2-9048-4910-9b91-63454d7d8ff3",
                                "sense_id": "9606747f-dc02-349c-8493-934c8cd74f51",
                                "text": "Later though, after about two weeks in untime, Finn began to get confused, and my job changed to simply keeping him straight."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e11c846b-da1d-465b-80ed-49a8f45688d9",
                                "sense_id": "9606747f-dc02-349c-8493-934c8cd74f51",
                                "text": "Nirvana, as we shall see, is a time rather than a place, but it is better still described as an un-time."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ff56cd9-855c-49f0-818a-73e5d82c9fd0",
                                "sense_id": "9606747f-dc02-349c-8493-934c8cd74f51",
                                "text": "While everyone else is frozen in untime Katie is unaffected and therefore acts as his sidekick in his efforts to avert disaster, death and devastation—[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8c7cb3f1-a845-3cca-b2df-182adae3d13b",
                        "entry_id": "a32b223f-83a8-34d9-a26b-f8d2d44772c7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A wrong time; an unsuitable or improper time."
                        ],
